{"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}]},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus()"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The sparse-set storage","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The archetype storage","anchor":"The-archetype-storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops all tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What the numbers say","anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass (","type":"text"},{"code":"make benchmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", see ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Case"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sparse set"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Archetype","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A)"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2.5 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4.3 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"31 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.4 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"23 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"3.6 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1.3 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"227 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Random "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"345 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 180 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4 900 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 730 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row","alignments":["left","right","right"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"code":"IterOnlyOneComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity."}]}]}]},{"text":"Which storage to pick","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}]},{"text":"Differences you can observe","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Single-type spans.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Family spans.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the spans."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"https://github.com/SanderMertens/flecs/blob/master/docs/ComponentTraits.md":{"title":"component traits","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"component traits"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/default":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","abstract":[{"text":"The storage ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" uses by default: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"`default`","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","text":"Nexus","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"default","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/default"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values."}],"kind":"article","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Nexus","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Nexus","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus","type":"topic","title":"Nexus"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StorageKind"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StorageKind"}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"NexusEvent","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/archetype":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","abstract":[{"text":"One table per component set, a column per component type in every table, an index from entity to table and row.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"archetype","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind.archetype","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/archetype"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"title":"NexusEventDelegate"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","type":"topic","title":"FirebladeECS"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventmask","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventMask"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of events a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" subscribes to."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventMask"}],"title":"NexusEventMask"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick":{"title":"Which storage to pick","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","abstract":[],"kind":"section"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReadingAndWritingComponents":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read a copy, replace a component or change it in place."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/readingandwritingcomponents","type":"topic","title":"Reading and writing components"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Entity/identifier":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/entity\/identifier","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The unique entity identifier."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EntityIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS16EntityIdentifierV"}],"title":"identifier"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus."}],"kind":"article","title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say":{"title":"What the numbers say","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStora